<!--
  Hero (the commander) and troop characters of Commander Battle's Battanian troop classes
  (cb_mpclassdivisions_battania.xml), merged into Native's mpcharacters.xml (MPCharacters, MultiplayerGame only). All new
  ids: the stock characters stay untouched. Same rules as cb_mpcharacters_vlandia.xml:
  - default_group sets the class group, hence the role (Infantry, Ranged, Cavalry, HorseArcher).
  - Bots draw every equipment slot from a random roster of their character (Equipment.GetRandomEquipmentElements with a
    seed rolls again per slot), so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters vary the looks,
    never the loadout. Weapons, horse and shield are the same in every roster; the weapon setups (perks) swap them.
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon (or bow), Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm, Item3 free.
  - The rosters carry weapon setup 0, the culture's signature: infantry spear + targe (round shield), archers longbow +
    two-handed sidearm, cavalry spear or lance + Battanian large (big round) shield.
  - Every roster also has a Cape: Battanian cloaks and shoulder pieces, light ones on the light weights, mail
    shoulders on the heavy. A cape adds to body armour, so each class keeps capes of about the same value.
  - Gear tiers: light = clan levy (highland cloth, leather or padded coats, a real helmet, a shield, a proper weapon and
    a sidearm); medium = mail-clad clan warriors (Battanian mail or light scale, cheek-guard helmets); heavy = oathsworn
    and fians (the culture's best mail and scale, crowned and ridged helmets, the best weapons and the strongest
    longbow). Battania is a step lighter than Vlandia and Sturgia at each weight: the oathsworn stay below the
    Vlandian dismounted knights and the Sturgian varyags.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml.
-->
